4.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {D3}

White’s D1–D2 group has the single liberty D3.  Any first move ≠ D3 lets Black play D3 and capture D1–D2 at once, so a saving first move is forced.  
After W D3 the white group C3–C4–D1–D2–D3 is alive with liberties D4,C5 and White threatens the left-hand Black complex.  B1 is now a net-threat on C1–C2 and, with A3/A4, a forcing net on the A1–A2–B3–B4–C1–C2 complex.  In every legal Black reply Black is forced to fill B2 or to connect the left groups, after which A4 – or the capture of the C1–C2 group by B2 – is a forced capture.  D3 is therefore the unique first move that both saves the atari and initiates a forced kill.

